# The AIEP Python stack. Hand-edited source file.
#
#   make lock      # uv pip compile requirements.in -o requirements.lock
#   make setup     # conda env + uv pip install -r requirements.lock
#
# Do NOT `pip install -r` this file directly — install requirements.lock, which pins
# every transitive dependency. This file only states the direct dependencies and the
# floor each one needs.
#
# The interpreter and the graphviz binary come from environment.yml (conda). Everything
# below is installed by uv, inside that conda env.
#
# Colab: ignore this file. Each notebook's portable setup cell installs what its lab needs.

# CPU torch wheels by default. requirements-gpu.in overrides this for CUDA machines.
#
# `--index-strategy unsafe-best-match` is required, not optional. uv defaults to
# first-index-wins to prevent dependency-confusion attacks: a package found on the
# PyTorch index is never looked up on PyPI, even if PyPI has a newer version. That
# default makes torchmetrics unresolvable here, because the PyTorch index carries an old
# copy of it. Both indexes below are first-party and trusted, so considering versions
# from both is the correct behaviour in this case.
# `make lock` passes --index-strategy unsafe-best-match for this reason; it is a CLI
# flag, not a directive a requirements file can carry, so do not add it below.
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu

